# PHASE 14 — Test Again Flow

The user should be able to restart the test.

When clicked:

```text id="50fg2x"
Results
   ↓
Reset UI
   ↓
Clear temporary values
   ↓
Initialize new test session
   ↓
Start Test
```

### Requirements

* No page reload required.
* No duplicate test processes.
* Previous network requests cleaned up.
* Previous timers cleaned up.
* Speedometer resets.
* Results reset correctly.

---

# PHASE 15 — Error States

Create simple, user-friendly error handling.

## Backend Unavailable

```text id="kwc3xj"
Unable to connect to the speed test server.

Please try again.

[ Try Again ]
```

## Network Error

```text id="dy6s46"
Your connection changed during the test.

[ Try Again ]
```

## Unexpected Error

```text id="c96jxg"
Something went wrong while testing your connection.

[ Try Again ]
```

### Requirements

* Never expose raw backend errors.
* Log technical errors safely.
* Stop active timers.
* Clean up active requests.
* Allow retry.

---

# PHASE 16 — Speedometer Refinement

The speedometer should be visually clean and functional.

## Requirements

* Use actual speed-test measurements.
* Smooth transitions.
* No random movement.
* No fake values.
* Correct unit handling.
* Reset between tests.
* Stop after completion.

### Data Flow

```text id="w1bplx"
Real Measurement
      ↓
Speed Test State
      ↓
Animation Layer
      ↓
Speedometer
```

The animation layer may smooth values but must not change the measurement result.

---

# PHASE 17 — Visual Design System

Create a consistent visual system.

## Design Direction

Use:

* Clean dark interface.
* Limited glass effects.
* Subtle borders.
* High contrast.
* Clear typography.
* Consistent spacing.

Avoid:

* Excessive blur.
* Neon everywhere.
* Heavy gradients.
* Over-animated UI.

