# PHASE 27 — Performance Optimization

The frontend must not interfere significantly with speed measurements.

## Check

* Unnecessary React renders.
* Heavy animations.
* Large dependencies.
* Memory leaks.
* Duplicate API calls.
* Multiple active timers.
* Large images.
* Excessive background effects.

### Important

```text id="zc6kx4"
Speed Test Running
        ↓
Frontend Must Stay Lightweight
        ↓
Avoid Affecting Device Performance
```

---

# PHASE 28 — Backend Integration Validation

Verify:

```text id="o6w4ry"
Next.js Frontend
        ↓
Speed Test Service
        ↓
LibreSpeed Client/API
        ↓
Railway Backend
```

Check:

* Production backend URL.
* Environment variables.
* CORS.
* HTTPS.
* Timeout behavior.
* Error responses.
* Server availability.
* No localhost production configuration.

---

# PHASE 29 — Security Review

Audit:

* Exposed environment variables.
* API keys.
* Public/private environment configuration.
* CORS.
* Rate limiting.
* Input validation.
* Contact form abuse.
* Error message exposure.
* Sensitive logging.

Do not expose backend infrastructure details to the client unnecessarily.

