# Final Execution Order for Antigravity

```text id="kwd39j"
PHASE 1
Repository Analysis
        ↓
PHASE 2
Architecture Refinement
        ↓
PHASE 3
Speed Test State Lifecycle
        ↓
PHASE 4
Configure Actual 7-Second Tests
        ↓
PHASE 5–7
Homepage + Core Speed Test UI
        ↓
PHASE 8–12
Progress + Download + Upload + Metrics
        ↓
PHASE 13–15
Results + Restart + Errors
        ↓
PHASE 16–17
Speedometer + Visual System
        ↓
PHASE 18–24
All Website Pages + Navigation + Footer
        ↓
PHASE 25–27
Responsive + Accessibility + Performance
        ↓
PHASE 28–29
Backend + Security Validation
        ↓
PHASE 30–31
Testing + Final Quality Audit
```

## Final Critical Requirement

**The implementation must configure the actual network measurement process so download and upload testing each run for approximately 7 seconds. Antigravity must verify the existing LibreSpeed configuration and apply the duration at the correct measurement layer—not merely display a 7-second frontend timer. The UI must remain simple, lightweight, and driven entirely by real test states and real measurement data.**
